@@ CIS-M-0004
disp: EXISTING_GROUP_NEEDS_EXPLICIT_FACET
nature: CHECKER_ACCEPTANCE_GATE (lexical detection of event handling)
appl: actor=check-instructions.mjs (maintainer/CI); action=fail a registered hook script that reads .hook_event_name but lacks the literal pattern === '<Event>'; trigger=running the instruction checker; modality=CHECKER FAILURE; scope=.claude/settings.json hooks and .claude/hooks scripts; exceptions=scripts that never read .hook_event_name are not tested; timing=maintenance/CI; enforcement=static code read, checker not executed; loading=maintenance script (not loaded into agent context)
match: FG-M-38b2281856
compared: FG-M-80646b7ff3 FG-M-54d1e6e5e9
rationale: check-instructions.mjs:300-304 verified. FG-M-38b2281856 already registers the gate 'a script dispatching on hook_event_name must handle each registered event'. The checker implements 'handle' as the lexical regex ===\s*'Event', so semantically correct dispatch (double quotes, switch/case) fails. This is a narrower acceptance boundary of an existing gate, not a separate obligation; recorded as a facet.
scenario: Replace event === 'PostToolUse' with event === "PostToolUse": runtime behaviour unchanged, FG-M-38b2281856's wording satisfied, but the checker fails.
conf: HIGH
facet: FG-M-38b2281856 | NEW_BEHAVIOR_BOUNDARY | The checker recognises event handling only by the literal pattern === '<Event>' (strict equality with a single-quoted event name); other dispatch spellings of a script that reads .hook_event_name fail the check.

@@ CIS-M-0005
disp: EXISTING_GROUP_NEEDS_EXPLICIT_FACET
nature: CHECKER_ACCEPTANCE_GATE (required-hook registration shape)
appl: actor=check-instructions.mjs (maintainer/CI); action=require one registration group whose matcher covers all required tools and which runs the required script; trigger=running the instruction checker; modality=CHECKER FAILURE; scope=.claude/settings.json; exceptions=empty, '*' or absent matcher counts as covering all tools; timing=maintenance/CI; enforcement=static code read, not executed; loading=maintenance script
match: FG-M-54d1e6e5e9
compared: FG-M-80646b7ff3
rationale: check-instructions.mjs:318-327 verified: groups.some(group => tools.every(...) && group runs script). FG-M-54d1e6e5e9 lists the required registrations ('on Bash|PowerShell') but not that coverage must sit in one group. Split registrations that cover every tool fail; recorded as an acceptance-boundary facet of the existing required-registration group.
scenario: Register dependency-guard for PreToolUse once with matcher Bash and once with matcher PowerShell: both tools covered, checker fails; a single Bash|PowerShell group passes.
conf: HIGH
facet: FG-M-54d1e6e5e9 | NEW_BEHAVIOR_BOUNDARY | Each required event/script must be registered in a single group whose matcher (split on '|') contains every required tool, or whose matcher is empty/'*'/absent; coverage spread across several groups fails the check.

@@ CIS-M-0006
disp: EXISTING_GROUP_NEEDS_EXPLICIT_FACET
nature: CHECKER_ACCEPTANCE_GATE (frontmatter parser shape for rule paths)
appl: actor=check-instructions.mjs (maintainer/CI); action=accept rule paths only as a block sequence of '- ' items; trigger=running the instruction checker on .claude/rules/*.md; modality=CHECKER FAILURE; scope=.claude/rules frontmatter; exceptions=none; timing=maintenance/CI; enforcement=static code read, not executed; host parsing of rule frontmatter not verified; loading=maintenance script
